Glass‑to‑metal adapters are hermetic sealing components that merge the insulating, low‑outgassing properties of glass with the mechanical strength and weldability of metal alloys such as Kovar, stainless steel or titanium. Their primary function is to provide a reliable transition between glass‑based optical or sensor elements and metal housings, ensuring vacuum integrity, electrical isolation or fluid containment under extreme thermal‑cycling and pressure‑differential conditions.
